{"content":[{"c":["TOWN CLERK*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["An official in municipal administration whose duties included those of scribe or secretary. He published the decrees of the civic authority but also acted as a liaison officer between the administration of a city and the Roman provincial government. In Ephesus he was held responsible for the riotous assembly in Paul’s day (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.19.35","r":"Acts.19.35","rawR":"Acts.19.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.19.35","value":"Acts.19.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 19:35"},") and had the power to impose a severe penalty. Fortunately, he was able to calm the assembly."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"TownClerk","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Acts 19:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.19.35","rawQueryValue":"Acts.19.35","sourceRefExact":"Acts.19.35"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"df8bb73cd6971359109782089fa927367fa1850033ecd0778dc56ec5267ff0f3","sourceItemName":"TownClerk","sourceItemOrder":219,"sourceMember":"Articles/T.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"TownClerk","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Town Clerk*","title":"Town Clerk*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}